 Summary\\n\\nPR #11991 (merged 2026-04-02) and PR #11857 added automatic app identification headers to OpenRouter requests:\\n- `HTTP-Referer: https://www.continue.dev/`\\n- `X-OpenRouter-Title: Continue`\\n- `X-OpenRouter-Categories: ide-extension`\\n\\nIssue #11923 was previously opened for this but was closed without the documentation actually being added to the docs.\\n\\n## Documentation Needed\\n\\nThe OpenRouter provider documentation at `docs/customize/model-providers/top-level/openrouter.mdx` should be updated to include:\\n\\n1. **App Identification section**: Explain that Continue automatically sends identification headers to OpenRouter\\n2. **Dashboard visibility**: Mention that users can see their Continue usage in OpenRouter's activity dashboard under the \\\"Continue\\\" app name\\n3. **Override capability**: Note that custom headers in `requestOptions.headers` can override these defaults if needed\\n\\n## Suggested Addition\\n\\nAdd a new section to the OpenRouter docs:\\n\\n```markdown\\n## App Identification\\n\\nContinue automatically sends identification headers with all OpenRouter requests:\\n- `HTTP-Referer: https://www.continue.dev/`\\n- `X-OpenRouter-Title: Continue`\\n- `X-OpenRouter-Categories: ide-extension`\\n\\nThese headers help identify Continue in [OpenRouter's activity dashboard](https://openrouter.ai/activity) and App Showcase. Your usage will appear under the \\\"Continue\\\" app.\\n\\nIf needed, you can override these headers using `requestOptions.headers` in your configuration.\\n```\\n\\n## Related PRs\\n\\n- #11991: feat(openrouter): send HTTP-Referer and X-Title headers in core/llm OpenRouter class\\n- #11857: feat(openrouter): send HTTP-Referer and X-Title headers to identify app\\n- Previous closed issue: #11923\\n\\n---\\n\\nGenerated with [Continue](https://continue.dev)\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Continue <noreply@continue.dev>\\nCo-authored-by: bekahhw <rhawrot@gmail.com>\",\n    \"closed_by\": null,\n    \"reactions\": {\n      \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/continuedev/continue/issues/12065/reactions\",\n      \"total_count\": 0,\n      \"+1\": 0,\n      \"-1\": 0,\n      \"laugh\": 0,\n      \"hooray\": 0,\n      \"confused\": 0,\n      \"heart\": 0,\n      \"rocket\": 0,\n      \"eyes\": 0\n    },\n    \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/continuedev/continue/issues/12065/timeline\",\n    \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n    \"state_reason\": null,\n    \"pinned_comment\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/continuedev/continue/issues/12064\",\n    \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/continuedev/continue\",\n    \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/continuedev/continue/issues/12064/labels{/name}\",\n    \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/continuedev/continue/issues/12064/comments\",\n    \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/continuedev/continue/issues/12064/events\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/continuedev/continue/pull/12064\",\n    \"id\": 4215708094,\n    \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOJm0kOc7QZNZb\",\n    \"number\": 12064,\n    \"title\": \"docs(openai): add Kelly Intelligence to OpenAI-compatible providers list\",\n    \"user\": {\n      \"login\": \"nicoletterankin\",\n      \"id\": 68830687,\n      \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjY4ODMwNjg3\",\n      \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/68830687?v=4\",\n      \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n      \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nicoletterankin\",\n      \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/nicoletterankin\",\n      \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nicoletterankin/followers\",\n      \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nicoletterankin/following{/other_user}\",\n      \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nicoletterankin/gists{/gist_id}\",\n      \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nicoletterankin/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n      \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nicoletterankin/subscriptions\",\n      \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nicoletterankin/orgs\",\n      \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nicoletterankin/repos\",\n      \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nicoletterankin/events{/privacy}\",\n      \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/nicoletterankin/received_events\",\n      \"type\": \"User\",\n      \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n      \"site_admin\": false\n    },\n    \"labels\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": 8578182706,\n        \"node_id\": \"LA_kwDOJm0kOc8AAAAB_0yuMg\",\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/continuedev/continue/labels/size:XS\",\n        \"name\": \"size:XS\",\n        \"color\": \"00ff00\",\n        \"default\": false,\n        \"description\": \"This PR changes 0-9 lines, ignoring generated files.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"state\": \"open\",\n    \"locked\": false,\n    \"assignees\": [\n\n    ],\n    \"milestone\": null,\n    \"comments\": 1,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-04-07T05:44:35Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-04-07T05:45:36Z\",\n    \"closed_at\": null,\n    \"assignee\": null,\n    \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n    \"type\": null,\n    \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n    \"draft\": false,\n    \"pull_request\": {\n      \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/continuedev/continue/pulls/12064\",\n      \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/continuedev/continue/pull/12064\",\n      \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/continuedev/continue/pull/12064.diff\",\n      \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/continuedev/continue/pull/12064.patch\",\n      \"merged_at\": null\n    },\n    \"body\": \"## Description\\n\\nOne-line addition to the **OpenAI API compatible providers** bullet list in `docs/customize/model-providers/top-level/openai.mdx`.\\n\\n[Kelly Intelligence](https://api.thedailylesson.com) is an OpenAI-compatible API with a built-in vocabulary RAG layer (162,000 words across 47 languages) and an AI tutor persona, built on top of Claude. It's operated by [Lesson of the Day, PBC](https://lotdpbc.com), a public benefit corporation building education infrastructure. The free tier requires no credit card.\\n\\nIt works with Continue out of the box using the existing `provider: openai` + `apiBase` pattern that's already documented on the same page — **no new provider integration, no code changes**, just one new bullet alongside KoboldCpp, LocalAI, vLLM, BerriAI/litellm, and Tetrate Agent Router Service.\\n\\n### Example config (uses existing `provider: openai` + `apiBase`)\\n\\n```yaml\\nname: My Config\\nversion: 0.0.1\\nschema: v1\\n\\nmodels:\\n  - name: Kelly Haiku\\n    provider: openai\\n    model: kelly-haiku\\n    apiBase: https://api.thedailylesson.com/v1\\n    apiKey: <YOUR_KELLY_API_KEY>\\n```\\n\\n### Try without an API key\\n\\nKelly Intelligence has a public `/v1/demo` endpoint for trying the API without any signup (5 requests/hour per IP):\\n\\n```bash\\ncurl -X POST https://api.thedailylesson.com/v1/demo \\\\\\n  -H \\\"Content-Type: application/json\\\" \\\\\\n  -d '{\\\"messages\\\":[{\\\"role\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"What does ephemeral mean?\\\"}]}'\\n```\\n\\nThis is the same wire format as `/v1/chat/completions` — useful for verifying the integration before adding a key to your Continue config.\\n\\n## AI Code Review\\n\\n- **Team members only**: AI review runs automatically when PR is opened or marked ready for review\\n- Team members can also trigger a review by commenting `@continue-review`\\n\\n## Checklist\\n\\n- [x] I've read the [contributing guide](https://github.com/continuedev/continue/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\\n- [x] The relevant docs, if any, have been updated or created\\n- [x] The relevant tests, if any, have been updated or created (n/a — docs-only, single bullet addition)\\n\\n## Screen recording or screenshot\\n\\nn/a — single-line documentation addition to an existing bullet list.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\nn/a — docs-only change, no code touched. The example config above has been verified end-to-end against the live `https://api.thedailylesson.com/v1` endpoint.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Note on positioning:** Kelly Intelligence is **complementary** to direct provider access, not a replacement for the official Anthropic SDK. It's the right fit when an application needs the OpenAI wire format **and** vocabulary / language-learning RAG features without building that data layer in-house.\\n\\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\\n---\\n## Summary by cubic\\nAdd Kelly Intelligence to the OpenAI-compatible providers list in `docs/customize/model-providers/top-level/openai.mdx`. It works via the existing `provider: openai` + `apiBase` pattern.\\n\\n<sup>Written for commit fa22e26a6cf431283b88c2c611a9027286fe61f0. Summary will update on new commits.</sup>\\n\\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\\n\\n\",\n    \"closed_by\": null,\n    \"reactions\": {\n      \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/continuedev/continue/issues/12064/reactions\",\n      \"total_count\": 0,\n      \"+1\": 0,\n      \"-1\": 0,\n      \"laugh\": 0,\n      \"hooray\": 0,\n      \"confused\": 0,\n      \"heart\": 0,\n      \"rocket\": 0,\n      \"eyes\": 0\n    },\n    \"timeline_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/continuedev/continue/issues/12064/timeline\",\n    \"performed_via_github_app\": null,\n    \"state_reason\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/continuedev/continue/issues/12063\",\n    \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/continuedev/continue\",\n    \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/continuedev/continue/issues/12063/labels{/name}\",\n    \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/continuedev/continue/issues/12063/comments\",\n    \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/continuedev/continue/issues/12063/events\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/continuedev/continue/pull/12063\",\n    \"id\": 4215671068,\n    \"node_id\": \"PR_kwDOJm0kOc7QZHC4\",\n    \"number\": 12063,\n    \"title\": \"[codex] fix(vscode): run commands in remote terminals\",\n    \"user\": {\n      \"login\": \"yzlu0917\",\n      \"id\": 153152554,\n      \"node_id\": \"U_kgDOCSDsKg\",\n      \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/153152554?v=4\",\n      \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n      \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/yzlu0917\",\n      \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/yzlu0917\",\n      \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/yzlu0917/followers\",\n      \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/yzlu0917/following{/other_user}\",\n      \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/yzlu0917/gists{/gist_id}\",\n      \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/yzlu0917/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n      \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/yzlu0917/subscriptions\",\n      \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/yzlu0917/orgs\",\n      \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/yzlu0917/repos\",\n      \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/yzlu0917/events{/privacy}\",\n      \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/yzlu0917/received_events\",\n      \"type\": \"User\",\n      \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n      \"site_admin\": false\n    },\n    \"labels\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": 8578182731,\n        \"node_id\": \"LA_kwDOJm0kOc8AAAAB_0yuSw\",\n        \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/continuedev/continue/labels/size:L\",\n        \"name\": \"size:L\",\n        \"color\": \"eb9500\",\n        \"default\": false,\n        \"description\": \"This PR changes 100-499 lines, ignoring generated files.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"state\": \"open\",\n    \"locked\": false,\n    \"assignees\": [\n\n    ],\n    \"milestone\": null,\n    \"comments\": 0,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-04-07T05:35:14Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-04-07T05:42:30Z\",\n    \"closed_at\": null,\n    \"assignee\": null,\n    \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n    \"type\": null,\n    \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n    \"draft\": false,\n    \"pull_request\": {\n      \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/continuedev/continue/pulls/12063\",\n      \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/continuedev/continue/pull/12063\",\n      \"diff_url\": \"https://github.com/continuedev/continue/pull/12063.diff\",\n      \"patch_url\": \"https://github.com/continuedev/continue/pull/12063.patch\",\n      \"merged_at\": null\n    },\n    \"body\": \"## Summary\\n- route `VsCodeIde.runCommand()` through a dedicated terminal helper\\n- create new terminals with `workbench.action.terminal.new` when the workspace is remote, so SSH/devcontainer/codespaces commands start on the correct machine\\n- always send commands with a trailing newline and add regression tests for local reuse, remote creation, and named remote terminal reuse\\n\\n## Why\\n`VsCodeIde.runCommand()` currently has two remote-terminal bugs:\\n- `sendText(command, false)` types the command but never executes it\\n- `createTerminal()` from the UI-side extension host creates a local terminal instead of a remote one\\n\\nThat breaks `/cmd`, Ollama/Lemonade startup helpers, and any terminal-tool fallback path in remote workspaces.\\n\\n## Validation\\n- ran `npm test -- src/util/runCommandInTerminal.vitest.ts` in `extensions/vscode`\\n- ran `git diff --check`\\n- ran `npm run tsc:check` in `extensions/vscode` and only hit existing repo issues unrelated to this patch:\\n  - `../../core/llm/llms/OpenRouter.ts`: missing `OPENROUTER_HEADERS` export\\n  - `src/extension.ts`: missing `./.buildTimestamp` declaration\\n\\nCloses #10542\\n\\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\\n---\\n## Summary by cubic\\nFixes command execution in VS Code terminals for remote workspaces by creating remote-aware terminals and ensuring commands run. Restores `/cmd`, Ollama/Lemonade startup helpers, and terminal tool fallbacks in SSH/devcontainers/Codespaces.\\n\\n- **Bug Fixes**\\n  - Route `VsCodeIde.runCommand()` through `runCommandInTerminal`; when remote, create terminals via `workbench.action.terminal.new\n\n... [1472 lines truncated] ...",
